  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaria - Namibia (01-Jan-2018-31-Dec-2020)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Namibia, Malaria, Ministry of Health and Social Services of Namibia (MOH)This program has the following goals: Goal: To achieve zero local malaria  cases in Namibia by 2022. The objectives of this program are: To protect 100% of targetted population living in malarious areas with at least one appropriate vector control intervention.  All suspected malaria cases are tested and 100% of confirmed malaria cases treated according to the national guidelines.  By 2020, at least 85% of the population utilize malaria interventions (LLINS or IRS).  Fully functional malaria surveillance system for evidence-based action in all districts by 2019.  To provide effective leadership and coordination for optimal implementation of malaria intervention at all levels</narrative>
  </description>
